  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In 1947, after the reported crash of a flying saucer near Roswell, New Mexico, a red-haired colonel is said to have shown up at the Roswell army air base, taken charge and had the wreckage cleared away. The physicist John Brandenburg tells Michels he heard this from Roswell veterans, who said the colonel arrived \"barking orders.\" It would suggest that someone from outside took control of the base to manage the recovery."
